1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,400
A story is a wish for a better world. How do we split that wish?

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,767
Three friends want to get home after dinner.

3
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:12,900
If we already know the answer, divide its structure: database, API, screen.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,167
But software development is also about discovering the answer.

5
00:00:16,167 --> 00:00:22,200
Problem decomposition splits customer problems: find the next train; check the fare; find a step-free route.

6
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:26,033
Two premises: seek smaller customer problems before choosing solutions.

7
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:28,633
A plan is an attempt, not a guarantee.

8
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:32,067
Two goals. First: deliver value and feedback.

9
00:00:32,067 --> 00:00:35,867
One small story crosses the product. Now they know when the next train leaves.

10
00:00:35,867 --> 00:00:37,933
Their reaction changes the next step.

11
00:00:37,933 --> 00:00:40,167
Just enough, just in time to learn.

12
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:43,067
Second: change direction without waste or damage.

13
00:00:43,067 --> 00:00:46,333
Keep completed value; leave later stories unstarted.

14
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:49,133
Nothing half-built to abandon. Nothing broken to repair.

15
00:00:49,133 --> 00:00:55,533
Four principles. Three Vs: valuable to customers, visible in their world, vertical through the product.

16
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:58,733
One-piece flow: finish one customer outcome together.

17
00:00:58,733 --> 00:01:03,367
Repeat at smaller scales: stories, scenarios, implementation slices.

18
00:01:03,367 --> 00:01:05,300
Every commit is your last commit.

19
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:13,367
Strive for useful value now; serve today's purpose or an already documented need, including product health, not merely prepare the next commit.

20
00:01:13,367 --> 00:01:17,767
Care for the whole product. Assimilate each splash into a coherent design.

21
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:22,467
Customer value now; speculative future potential at a cost: option value.

22
00:01:22,467 --> 00:01:25,733
Unused features can add complexity and close alternatives.

23
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:31,567
Smaller problems. Useful impacts. Freedom to choose again.
